  description="FutureClarity Technologies wants everyone to be able to use its website. The standard we aim for, how we test, and how to reach us if something gets in your way."
>
  <p>
    We want everyone to be able to use futureclaritytechnologies.com, including people who use a
    screen reader, a keyboard, voice control or magnification.
  </p>

  <h2>What we aim for</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA. The site is built
    with a clear page structure and headings, labeled form fields, text that contrasts with its
    background, visible focus for keyboard users, a "Skip to content" link, and no flashing content.
    It also respects your device's "reduce motion" setting.
  </p>

  <h2>How we test</h2>
  <p>
    We check the site with automated accessibility testing (axe) and by using it with only a keyboard,
    on desktop and phone screen sizes, and we re-check when we make changes.
  </p>

  <h2>If something doesn't work for you</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us and we'll fix it, or get you what you need another way, such as booking your audit over
    the phone. Email <a href="mailto:beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com">beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com</a>
    or call or text <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>. We aim to reply within two business
    days.
  </p>

  <h2>The sites we build</h2>
  <p>
    The websites and dashboards we build for clients are held to the same standard, and we're happy
    to talk through accessibility for yours.
  </p>
</Doc>
